{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Completion verifier reads a stale ticket snapshot — CONFIRMED DEFECT (plus a second, independent bare-FAIL defect)\n\n## Disposition (investigation complete)\n\nHypothesis 1 (**staleness defect**) is CONFIRMED; hypothesis 3 (**a non-itemized FAIL is\nindistinguishable from \"no verdict obtainable\"**) is CONFIRMED as a SECOND, independent defect.\nHypothesis 2 (deliberate anti-gaming snapshot) is REJECTED: the pin is deliberate, but its\ndocumented purpose is reproducibility/signability and its own docstring states the goal is to pin\n\"the shared store, **not a stale local copy**\" (`src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:546-548`) —\nstaleness is contrary to intent, not the intent.\n\n### Root cause 1 — the close path pins the ticket store with no fetch\n\n`close_precheck` calls the verifier with `fetch=False`\n(`src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:505-512`), justified in its own comment (`:502-504`) only\nfor the CODE ref (`HEAD`, always local). But `resolve_gate_handle` threads the same flag into the\nTICKET store pin (`src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py:115`), and in `materialize_tickets`\n(`src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:568-576`) `fetch=False` skips `origin/tickets` and pins the\nmain repo's local `refs/heads/tickets` — a mirror that only advances on fetch. `.tickets-tracker/`\nis a SEPARATE repository, so that mirror is arbitrarily stale (measured here: 6757 commits behind).\n\nReproduced deterministically, no LLM call:\n\n    materialize_tickets(fetch=False) -> show_ticket(cb91) == {status: open,        comments: 0}\n    materialize_tickets(fetch=True)  -> show_ticket(cb91) == {status: in_progress, comments: 2}\n\n`status: open` + `comments: []` is verbatim what incident 1's stored `COMPLETION_VERDICT` cited.\n\n### Root cause 1b — the two halves of the gate read different stores\n\nThe fenced context handed to the model is assembled from the LIVE store (`gate_ops.py:174,190`),\nwhile the model's own `show_ticket` reads the PINNED snapshot (`runner.py:335-337`). The prompt\nlabels the context `<untrusted_ticket_context>` and names `show_ticket` authoritative\n(`reviewers/completion_verifier.md:26-28`), so the model correctly preferred the stale snapshot.\n\n### Root cause 2 — a FAIL with no findings is fabricated, not reported\n\n`reconcile_verdict` (`src/rebar/llm/completion.py:454-467`) coerces any non-`PASS` verdict to\n`FAIL`, then, when `findings` is empty, SYNTHESIZES a placeholder criterion `(unspecified)`.\nIncident 3's stored verdict shows exactly that. Unlike plan-review (unsigned `INDETERMINATE`,\nexit 2), completion verification cannot say \"I could not obtain a verdict\".\n\n## Implementation plan\n\n1. **Pin the ticket store at the LIVE store's own HEAD.** `materialize_tickets`\n   (`repo_snapshot.py:534`) resolves the sha from the live tracker repo (`.tickets-tracker`) HEAD\n   when that repo is present — the state every other rebar read sees — so the pin is\n   current-at-close by construction and the gate's two halves stop disagreeing. Still\n   immutable-by-sha and signable. `fetch` keeps its meaning (\"may I touch the network?\") and is\n   applied uniformly to every caller:\n   - `fetch=True` (`review-plan` via `operations.py:203`, standalone `verify-completion`, MCP):\n     force an UN-throttled reconverge of the tracker with `origin/tickets` (the existing\n     `_store.sync` implementation `reads.ensure_fresh` uses, called so the <=1/min marker is\n     bypassed). `reconverge` returns `None` on success AND on every failure/early-out, so it\n     yields no usable signal; `materialize_tickets` therefore CONFIRMS the result itself with an\n     explicit `git -C <tracker> merge-base --is-ancestor <remote>/tickets HEAD`. Exit 0 (HEAD is\n     at-or-ahead) => pin tracker HEAD. Non-zero, or the fetch / `rev-parse <remote>/tickets`\n     failing => fall back to today's exact behaviour, `resolve_ref(f\"{remote}/tickets\",\n     fetch=True)`. The \"no content visible today is lost\" invariant therefore holds\n     unconditionally, not only when a throttle window happens to be open.\n   - `fetch=False` (close path): pin tracker HEAD as-is — current-at-close, never the stale mirror.\n   - Tracker repo absent (CI, checkout-less): unchanged `origin/tickets` -> local-branch chain.\n2. **Give completion verification a \"no verdict obtainable\" channel.** Indeterminacy is carried\n   as a NEW framework-set boolean `verdict_obtainable` on the verdict, NOT a third verdict token:\n   the `{PASS, FAIL}` vocabulary, its normalizing validator, and fail-closed blocking all stay\n   intact, and no prompt/contract token can be coerced away. Touch points, all of them:\n   - `reconcile_verdict` (`completion.py:442`): when a non-PASS verdict carries zero `findings`\n     AND zero `criteria`, set `verdict_obtainable=false` and emit a finding that says the verifier\n     produced no usable verdict (a verifier fault) instead of the fabricated `(unspecified)`\n     criterion. `verdict` stays `FAIL` so every existing consumer still blocks.\n   - `gate_ops.completion_reconcile` (`workflow/gate_ops.py:297`) — the workflow close-gate path\n     that also stamps `certifiable`: inherits the marker automatically because it delegates to\n     `reconcile_verdict`; assert that with a test. A `verdict_obtainable=false` verdict is never\n     certifiable and never signs, exactly as any FAIL today.\n   - `completion_sidecar` (`completion_sidecar.py:323`): the marker rides through onto the durable\n     record so a fault is queryable after the fact rather than looking like an unmet criterion.\n   - `close_precheck.py:543`: check `verdict_obtainable` BEFORE the `!= PASS` branch and route it\n     to a distinct message naming it a verifier fault, with retryable exit 11 instead of 1.\n   - `_cli/_llm_commands.py:383-389` — the standalone `rebar verify-completion` exit mapping,\n     which today flattens every non-PASS verdict to exit 1: route `verdict_obtainable=false` to\n     the same retryable exit 11 `_llm_error_exit_code` already uses, so a verifier fault is\n     retryable regardless of entry point (close gate or standalone CLI).\n   - `schemas/completion_verdict.schema.json`: document the optional boolean.\n3. **Fix the misleading wording at its real sites.** The \"does not exist\" phrasing is\n   model-generated, so there is nothing to delete from the prompt; instead\n   (a) `reviewers/completion_verifier.md` gains an explicit instruction that an absence observed\n   via `show_ticket` must be reported as \"not visible in the ticket snapshot I read\", never as a\n   claim the record does not exist, and (b) the framework-authored\n   `COMPLETION_REMEDIATION_GUIDANCE` (`completion.py:54`) is reworded to match.\n4. **Document the ticket-store pin** in `docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md` (which today documents only\n   the code snapshot) and cross-reference from `docs/plan-review-gate.md`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] [operator-attested] The investigation is settled and durably recorded on this ticket: the\n      `show_ticket` read path and its exact pin point, and the verdict (staleness defect, NOT a\n      deliberate review-time snapshot). Evidence: the \"Disposition\", \"Root cause 1\", \"Root cause\n      1b\" and \"Root cause 2\" sections of this description, each carrying file:line citations.\n      This AC is already satisfied by the text above; the remaining ACs are the code end-states.\n- [ ] The pinned ticket snapshot reflects the live store at close time, with a regression test\n      that fails before the fix.\n- [ ] The `fetch=True` consumers are covered: a regression test proves a snapshot taken with\n      `fetch=True` still contains everything `origin/tickets` holds (including via the\n      confirm-or-fall-back path), so no content visible today is lost. Tracker-repo-absent\n      environments keep the existing resolution.\n- [ ] A non-PASS verdict with no itemized criteria sets `verdict_obtainable=false` and is reported\n      as a verifier fault with a distinct message and retryable exit, not as a fabricated unmet\n      criterion — with a regression test covering `reconcile_verdict` and the workflow path.\n- [ ] The unmet-criterion diagnostic distinguishes \"not present\" from \"not visible in the\n      snapshot read\".\n- [ ] The ticket-store pin is documented for users in `docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md`.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786587767251008001,"uuid":"9999efb7-1ef8-4efb-8148-9d9f0349d5bf"}